cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use geophylo, please cite it as below, and cite the ICS International Chronostratigraphic Chart as required by its CC BY 4.0 license (see the references list and NOTICE)."
title: "geophylo: reproducible geological timescale axes for Matplotlib, with an explicit coordinate-semantics contract and version-pinned ICS snapshots"
abstract: >-
  Geological timescale axes for Matplotlib: reproducible ICS snapshot access,
  linear geological timescale axes for timetrees and stratigraphic plots, and
  radial geological time rings, with explicit coordinate-semantics contracts.
authors:
  - family-names: Zeng
    given-names: Zichao
    email: zengzichao@sjtu.edu.cn
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6553-970X
    affiliation:
      name: School of Life Sciences and Biotechnology, Shanghai Jiao Tong University
      address: Shanghai
      country: CN
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZengZichao/GeoPhylo"
keywords:
  - geological timescale
  - phylogenetics
  - reproducible visualisation
  - Matplotlib
  - International Chronostratigraphic Chart
  - coordinate semantics
identifiers:
  # RESERVED — replace the value with the concept DOI that Zenodo mints at the
  # first GitHub release (it is version-agnostic and cites every later release).
  # See RELEASE.md, step 2. Do not publish with this placeholder in place.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.REPLACE_AT_FIRST_RELEASE
    description: >-
      Zenodo concept DOI for geophylo; to be minted at the first public release
      and recorded here. Until then, cite the repository URL and the version.
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "International Chronostratigraphic Chart"
    authors:
      - family-names: Cohen
        given-names: K. M.
      - family-names: Harper
        given-names: D. A. T.
      - family-names: Gibbard
        given-names: P. L.
      - family-names: Car
        given-names: N.
    year: 2025
    edition: "2026/06 (v2026-06.5)"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    url: "https://stratigraphy.org/chart"
    notes: >-
      The bundled snapshots are deterministic extracts of this chart; cite it
      alongside geophylo as required by CC BY 4.0. The reference year is the
      publication year of the Episodes paper describing the chart (2025); the
      chart edition the snapshots encode is 2026/06 (see the edition field).
